1
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:38,170
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,410 --> 00:01:40,940
[Episode 7]

3
00:01:41,479 --> 00:01:42,479
I'll take him

4
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,400
because we're

5
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,120
friends.

6
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:50,960
Good friends, huh?

7
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:54,920
Helping a good friend like that

8
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:57,520
is actually the spirit
behind poems dedicated to friends.

9
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:58,979
I think that's wonderful.

10
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,480
What do you think?

11
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:03,760
Sure.

12
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,639
All right, everyone,

13
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:10,500
hurry up and form your own groups.

14
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:12,760
Xiaotao,

15
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,800
want to be partners?

16
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,720
The two of us?

17
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:19,360
Yeah.

18
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,530
I look forward to working with you.

19
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,800
Great. Welcome, Senior!

20
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:56,040
[Selected Ci-Poetry of Nalan Xingde]

21
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:01,270
[Three Hundred Tang Poems,
Color Illustrated Edition]

22
00:03:01,270 --> 00:03:04,630
[Song of the Chaste Woman—Meng Jiao]
[Song of the Wanderer—Meng Jiao]

23
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:07,960
Come on,

24
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:11,170
let's start with a few poems
about friendship

25
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,500
and get in the mood.

26
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:15,690
[Song of the Chaste Woman—Meng Jiao]
[Song of the Wanderer—Meng Jiao]

27
00:03:16,970 --> 00:03:18,750
[Song of the Chaste Woman—Meng Jiao]
[Song of the Wanderer—Meng Jiao]

28
00:03:20,230 --> 00:03:21,840
[The River-Merchant's Wife:
A Letter—Li Bai]

29
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,320
"You rode to me on a bamboo horse.

30
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:25,520
Around the bed,
we played with green plums.

31
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,650
Together, we grew up in Changgan Lane.

32
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:32,160
Two innocent hearts,
with no mistrust between them."

33
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:41,560
Are you sure this has anything to do
with poems dedicated to friends?

34
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,930
[The River-Merchant's Wife:
A Letter—Li Bai]

35
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,570
Green plums? Two innocent hearts?

36
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,920
Your understanding of friendship

37
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:56,200
is too narrow.

38
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,560
Childhood sweethearts

39
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,920
can be friends, too.

40
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:00,640
When writing poetry,

41
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,360
you mustn't let this kind of thinking

42
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:03,560
limit you.

43
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:06,640
Okay.

44
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,560
"At fourteen, I became your wife.

45
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,960
I was too shy to smile..."

46
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,000
Have you ever had a childhood sweetheart

47
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,640
you were especially close to?

48
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:23,200
What does that have to do
with learning to write poetry?

49
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,720
Of course it does!

50
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,940
Just reading poems isn't enough.

51
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:30,200
Otherwise, you'll only be repeating
what others have written.

52
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,920
You have to draw on your own experiences

53
00:04:33,159 --> 00:04:35,840
and put yourself in the poet's shoes

54
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,970
to truly connect with their feelings.

55
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:40,820
Could she have figured out

56
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,760
that I'm Gu Xiaoli?

57
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,800
You have to be honest with yourself.

58
00:04:50,159 --> 00:04:51,280
Only then can your poetry

59
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:53,680
capture the true essence of your feelings.

60
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,720
I don't remember.

61
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,760
How could you not?

62
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:05,680
Either you had one

63
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,840
or you didn't.

64
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:15,800
So,

65
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:17,520
do you remember

66
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:19,120
your childhood sweetheart?

67
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,760
Oh, Xiaoli? He was the little boy

68
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,800
who used to live next door to us.

69
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:26,360
You used to bring him over
to our house for meals all the time.

70
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,240
Back then,

71
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,680
you'd follow him around everywhere,

72
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:29,680
calling out,

73
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,560
"Xiaoli. Xiaoli."

74
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,320
I really don't seem to remember him.

75
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:43,050
T-Then let's try another poem.

76
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:47,190
[Li Qingzhao: Her Life and Ci-Poems]

77
00:05:44,159 --> 00:05:45,620
Another one, another one.

78
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:47,080
This one.

79
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,120
This one.

80
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,120
If you don't remember her,

81
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:09,040
then even if she was once
in your heart,

82
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,360
she's not anymore.

83
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:15,000
What a false alarm.

84
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:20,900
[Read widely, read well]

85
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:24,400
Hello, Senior Fang Yu.

86
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:27,310
We're doing vocal exercises
at the Wetland Park tomorrow morning.

87
00:06:27,310 --> 00:06:28,120
I remember.

88
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:41,170
What do you think? Not a bad spot, right?

89
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,500
The air is fresh, the view is wide open,

90
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:44,840
and we won't have to hike up

91
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,900
a long mountain trail like last time.

92
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:48,780
Best of all,

93
00:06:48,810 --> 00:06:50,600
there are usually very few people here,

94
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,860
so you can practice freely

95
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:53,790
without feeling self-conscious.

96
00:06:55,810 --> 00:06:57,120
I think this place

97
00:06:57,150 --> 00:06:58,810
would be perfect for a picnic.

98
00:07:01,670 --> 00:07:03,040
Let's not think about that for now.

99
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,440
Let's focus on training.

100
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:08,510
All right, let's practice here, then.

101
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:14,230
Today, we're going to try
a different vocal warm-up technique.

102
00:07:14,230 --> 00:07:16,010
a—e—i—o—u

103
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:17,610
But remember,

104
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,800
it all starts with your breathing—

105
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,030
specifically, abdominal respiration.

106
00:07:21,030 --> 00:07:22,430
I'll demonstrate first.

107
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:24,620
Remember:

108
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:26,130
inhale through your nose
and exhale through your mouth.

109
00:07:26,130 --> 00:07:35,710
-a—e—i—o—u
-a—e—i—o—u

110
00:07:35,730 --> 00:07:39,810
Left, right, left, right.

111
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,060
Watch your breathing.

112
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,159
-Keep it steady.
-Isn't that Xiangxiang?

113
00:07:44,159 --> 00:07:44,880
Breathe.

114
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:47,810
Get your breathing under control.

115
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:58,840
What are you doing here
so early in the morning?

116
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:02,520
It's nice and cool today,

117
00:08:02,540 --> 00:08:04,540
so I brought everyone here for a run.

118
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:06,400
Is it cool?

119
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:09,440
Very cool.

120
00:08:09,650 --> 00:08:12,280
You drove over 20 minutes
just to run here?

121
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:13,880
Why not run at school?

122
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:20,720
What are you two doing here?

123
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:22,510
Vocal practice.

124
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,780
Come on, let's keep going.

125
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,160
Control your breathing.

126
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,159
Inhale.

127
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:36,280
Exhale.

128
00:08:37,679 --> 00:08:38,799
Inhale.

129
00:08:43,470 --> 00:08:46,040
Weren't you supposed to be training?

130
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:47,860
Why are you just standing there?

131
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,000
Let's go.

132
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:55,030
Come on.
Get your breathing under control.

133
00:08:55,030 --> 00:08:56,000
Inhale.

134
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,840
Exhale.

135
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:01,800
Inhale.

136
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:11,800
How is it cool?

137
00:09:11,930 --> 00:09:12,750
That's right.

138
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,500
Let your voice drop lower.

139
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:15,360
Arms!

140
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,440
Swing your arms!
Don't keep them on your stomach!

141
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,160
Keep going.

142
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,570
Swing them! Arms!

143
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,800
Push against my hand.

144
00:09:20,950 --> 00:09:21,640
Good!

145
00:09:21,930 --> 00:09:22,810
Shoulders!

146
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,030
-Keep going!
-Keep your arms swinging.

147
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:26,060
-Get them off your stomach!
-Keep going!

148
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:26,760
Arms!

149
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:27,840
Swing them!

150
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,720
Good, take a full breath.

151
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:30,920
Focus on your chest.

152
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,800
Project your voice to the farthest point.

153
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,460
Watch your arms.
Keep them off your stomach.

154
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:35,400
Come on, keep going.

155
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,400
Stay focused.

156
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,760
Left, right, left, right.

157
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,450
-Keep going!
-Left, right, left, right.

158
00:09:39,450 --> 00:09:40,440
Left, right, left, right.

159
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,760
Make sure you maintain
the correct technique and posture.

160
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,920
Come on. Your shoulders are too tense.

161
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:46,160
Shoulders!

162
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:47,690
Come on. Relax your shoulders.

163
00:09:47,690 --> 00:09:48,920
Straighten up.

164
00:09:48,990 --> 00:09:50,250
Relax your shoulders.

165
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,360
-Alright. Look straight ahead.
-Tuck your chin in.

166
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,840
Tuck your chin in yourself.

167
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,320
Head up. Good.

168
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,670
Chin, chin. Keep it tucked.

169
00:09:55,670 --> 00:09:57,070
-Alright. Look straight ahead.
-Left, right, left, right.

170
00:09:57,070 --> 00:09:57,810
Head up.

171
00:09:57,830 --> 00:09:59,490
-Head up, chest out!
-Head up.

172
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,510
Kong Fang, raise your shoulders.

173
00:10:01,510 --> 00:10:02,080
Relax.

174
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:02,800
Kong Fang, run properly!

175
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:03,440
-What are you doing?
-Look straight ahead.

176
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,440
Looking for special treatment?

177
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,420
Keep your shoulders up!

178
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:06,000
Come on.

179
00:10:06,650 --> 00:10:07,250
Your chin.

180
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:08,590
Chin, watch your chin.

181
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:10,520
Alright. Look straight ahead.

182
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,120
Look straight ahead.

183
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:12,050
Keep your chin tucked.

184
00:10:12,050 --> 00:10:12,820
Stay focused.

185
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:13,840
Left, right, left, right.

186
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:16,180
Peter Piper picked
a peck of pickled peppers.

187
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:17,300
Ready, go!

188
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,770
Peter Piper picked
a peck of pickled peppers.

189
00:10:20,770 --> 00:10:23,560
A peck of pickled peppers
Peter Piper picked.

190
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:26,400
A peck of pickled peppers
Peter Piper picked.

191
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:30,760
Senior,

192
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:33,200
you really thought ahead!

193
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:35,000
The weather's great,

194
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,480
and we don't often
get a chance like this.

195
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,480
Consider it a little reward for you.

196
00:10:43,030 --> 00:10:44,960
All right, take a break right here.

197
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:46,640
I'm about to pass out.

198
00:10:46,930 --> 00:10:48,960
Chen Yu, lead them through some stretches.

199
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,390
-Let's take a break.
-Come on, take a breather.

200
00:10:51,390 --> 00:10:52,160
Xiangxiang,

201
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,460
have a seat.

202
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,860
Do you have any water left?

203
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:02,680
Take this.

204
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,080
Thank you.

205
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:09,620
Aren't you going to get something to eat?

206
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:11,650
We'll eat in a bit. Help yourselves.

207
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:12,360
Okay.

208
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,310
Come on, have something to eat.

209
00:11:15,310 --> 00:11:16,160
Thank you.

210
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:24,360
Is there anything to eat?

211
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,920
Senior,

212
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:31,160
why don't we

213
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:32,920
invite them over to eat with us?

214
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:33,920
There's so much food—

215
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,520
we couldn't possibly
finish it all ourselves.

216
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:56,040
Do you have any water left?

217
00:12:02,830 --> 00:12:05,640
Senior, can you open this for me?

218
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,940
-This is good.
-Is there any more of that?

219
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,480
Do you have any more of that?

220
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:27,140
Give me some. Let me try a bite.

221
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:30,630
-It's so hot!
-Who would want

222
00:12:30,630 --> 00:12:32,340
to have a picnic in this heat?

223
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:34,160
It's scorching.

224
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:02,520
Why is my heart

225
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:05,040
racing this time?

226
00:13:27,050 --> 00:13:29,210
Senior, are you okay?

227
00:13:30,850 --> 00:13:31,800
I'm fine.

228
00:13:39,050 --> 00:13:41,680
Senior, does it hurt less now?

229
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:43,040
It's okay. Much better.

230
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:47,220
Be more careful next time.

231
00:13:47,220 --> 00:13:48,000
Thanks.

232
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:49,800
Let's go.

233
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:50,780
It's okay, no need.

234
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:51,980
I can manage on my own.

235
00:13:54,390 --> 00:13:55,560
-We'll take care of it.
-You don't have to stand on ceremony.

236
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:56,120
-You don't have to stand on ceremony.
-This way.

237
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:56,840
It's okay.

238
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:59,000
-It's okay.
-You don't have to stand on ceremony.

239
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,360
I can manage on my own. I'm fine.

240
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,880
It's the least we can do.

241
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,140
Where is everyone?

242
00:14:08,510 --> 00:14:10,510
They took Fang Yu over there to rest.

243
00:14:34,230 --> 00:14:35,110
How about this?

244
00:14:35,950 --> 00:14:37,120
Let's see if you've made any progress

245
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,480
these past few days.

246
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:41,770
Recite a couple of lines of poetry
to suit the occasion.

247
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:48,760
"Someone is on my mind, yet
we're strangers despite being so close.

248
00:14:49,290 --> 00:14:52,520
Something weighs on my heart,
deep within."

249
00:14:52,710 --> 00:14:55,280
That's Bai Juyi's "Night Rain."

250
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:00,680
Didn't Bai Juyi write that poem

251
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:02,520
for his childhood sweetheart?

252
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:04,760
Could it be that he...

253
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,780
"Drifting clouds, a wanderer's thoughts;
setting sun, an old friend's love."

254
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:13,240
The sunset is infinitely beautiful,
yet dusk is drawing near.

255
00:15:15,990 --> 00:15:18,580
So there's "Seeing Off a Friend"
about friendship,

256
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:20,980
and "A Short Poem on the Ancient Plain"
about personal feelings.

257
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:22,240
I was overthinking it.

258
00:15:23,430 --> 00:15:24,430
What do you think?

259
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:26,560
Not bad.

260
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,480
Senior,

261
00:15:53,910 --> 00:15:55,570
have you thought of anything?

262
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:58,040
Not much yet.

263
00:15:59,650 --> 00:16:01,600
Why don't we talk

264
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:04,040
and learn about each other's interests?

265
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:05,040
Sure.

266
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:06,680
[Remarks on Ci Poetry]

267
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:11,320
Senior, do you watch TV dramas?

268
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:12,480
I do.

269
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:14,300
I revisit shows like
"Romance of the Three Kingdoms"

270
00:16:14,300 --> 00:16:15,460
and "Dream of the Red Chamber"

271
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:16,760
from time

272
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:17,680
to time.

273
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:18,880
And I get something different

274
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:20,140
out of them every time.

275
00:16:22,300 --> 00:16:23,790
[Remarks on Ci Poetry]

276
00:16:25,780 --> 00:16:27,840
What about you?
What kind of shows do you watch?

277
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,870
I like lighthearted,

278
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:31,760
romantic love stories.

279
00:16:32,010 --> 00:16:34,930
You know, like when the female lead
meets the perfect guy,

280
00:16:34,930 --> 00:16:37,170
they fall in love,
and they live happily ever after.

281
00:16:37,170 --> 00:16:38,480
So sweet!

282
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:41,800
Recommend some to me sometime.

283
00:16:41,830 --> 00:16:43,230
I'll check them out, too.

284
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,640
Senior, do you play games?

285
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,280
Games?

286
00:16:59,490 --> 00:17:00,880
Does Sudoku count?

287
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:03,680
Yes...

288
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:04,960
Yes, it does.

289
00:17:08,530 --> 00:17:09,400
By the way,

290
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:11,390
there's a variety show
that's been pretty popular lately.

291
00:17:11,390 --> 00:17:12,560
Have you been following it?

292
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:13,560
What show?

293
00:17:13,579 --> 00:17:15,430
If you've watched it,
I'm sure I have, too.

294
00:17:15,430 --> 00:17:16,690
"National Treasure."

295
00:17:17,230 --> 00:17:18,270
I think the format

296
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:19,560
is pretty innovative.

297
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:20,520
Each episode features

298
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:21,800
a different historical figure

299
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,599
telling the stories
behind cultural relics.

300
00:17:22,940 --> 00:17:24,630
[Remarks on Ci Poetry]

301
00:17:23,849 --> 00:17:25,109
It really brings these artifacts

302
00:17:25,109 --> 00:17:26,119
to life

303
00:17:26,119 --> 00:17:27,920
for the audience.

304
00:17:29,310 --> 00:17:31,520
I'll check it out later.

305
00:17:34,210 --> 00:17:36,360
Let's get back to reading.

306
00:17:40,790 --> 00:17:41,720
Xiaotao.

307
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,320
Xiangxiang,

308
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:45,480
come here, come here.

309
00:17:49,190 --> 00:17:50,200
Senior,

310
00:17:51,030 --> 00:17:52,640
is your foot feeling better?

311
00:17:53,410 --> 00:17:54,210
Much better.

312
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:55,560
I can walk just fine now.

313
00:17:57,470 --> 00:17:59,130
How's the preparation going?

314
00:17:59,330 --> 00:18:00,330
Don't ask.

315
00:18:00,350 --> 00:18:04,280
My mind's been blank the whole time.
Not a single spark of inspiration.

316
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:05,620
What about you guys?

317
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:07,350
How's your preparation going?

318
00:18:07,590 --> 00:18:10,400
Honestly, we haven't
made much progress either.

319
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:12,800
Then why don't

320
00:18:12,950 --> 00:18:14,520
the four of us brainstorm together

321
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:16,110
and see if we can find some inspiration?

322
00:18:16,110 --> 00:18:17,690
Xiangxiang, you're the best.

323
00:18:17,690 --> 00:18:18,800
You'll help us out,

324
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:19,680
right?

325
00:18:20,050 --> 00:18:21,400
Of course.

326
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:25,320
Let's start

327
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:27,740
with the lines of poetry
we've each chosen.

328
00:18:27,970 --> 00:18:28,890
Mine is:

329
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:31,660
"The garden path
has never been swept for guests;

330
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:33,950
today, for you, my humble gate opens."

331
00:18:34,590 --> 00:18:35,390
Mine is,

332
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:37,880
"A true friend remains close at heart,
though worlds apart."

333
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:39,040
That's a good one.

334
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:42,070
Senior, what about you?

335
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:48,850
I haven't decided yet.

336
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:53,360
Senior Fang Yu?

337
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:58,980
"The perfume pouch was quietly untied,
the silken girdle softly loosened."

338
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:17,060
"The perfume pouch was quietly untied,
the silken girdle softly loosened."

339
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:18,920
Why does it sound so strange?

340
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,510
Even taken literally,

341
00:19:21,530 --> 00:19:22,650
it doesn't sound very innocent.

342
00:19:22,650 --> 00:19:23,410
Right?

343
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:25,840
You're all overthinking it.

344
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:27,840
Then what does it mean?

345
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:30,520
Xinyi, care to explain?

346
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:33,470
"The perfume pouch was quietly untied,
the silken girdle softly loosened"

347
00:19:33,470 --> 00:19:34,730
comes from Qin Guan's poem

348
00:19:34,730 --> 00:19:36,660
"Courtyard Full of Fragrance:
Clouds Veil the Mountain."

349
00:19:36,660 --> 00:19:39,110
People often mistake it
for an erotic description,

350
00:19:39,110 --> 00:19:40,960
but it actually refers to

351
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:42,740
untying the sash around one's waist

352
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:45,130
and removing a perfume pouch
to give to someone one loves.

353
00:19:45,130 --> 00:19:48,880
It subtly expresses romantic love
between a man and a woman.

354
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,020
But our theme is
poems dedicated to friends.

355
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:54,540
Aren't Xiaotao and Fang Yu

356
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:56,400
taking things a little too far?

357
00:19:57,730 --> 00:19:59,040
Let me tell you,

358
00:19:59,110 --> 00:20:01,420
at first, it was just Fang Yu and me,

359
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:03,310
and we had absolutely no inspiration.

360
00:20:03,310 --> 00:20:05,340
Then suddenly, we became a group of four,

361
00:20:05,340 --> 00:20:06,310
and along came this whole business with

362
00:20:06,310 --> 00:20:08,720
"The perfume pouch was quietly untied,
the silken girdle softly loosened."

363
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:10,700
It's not like that poem
was meant for me, was it?

364
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:12,670
Are you even going to focus
on preparing or not?

365
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:13,800
My bad. My bad.

366
00:20:19,110 --> 00:20:20,040
Eat.

367
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:33,460
"The perfume pouch was quietly untied,
the silken girdle softly loosened."

368
00:20:33,670 --> 00:20:35,200
Did Fang Yu really say that?

369
00:20:38,770 --> 00:20:40,680
Wait, don't take advantage
of my being bad at literature.

370
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:42,760
Isn't a silken girdle just a sash?

371
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:44,710
Why all the untying and loosening?

372
00:20:46,570 --> 00:20:47,360
Right?

373
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:48,670
A track team captain is one thing,

374
00:20:48,670 --> 00:20:50,770
but Fang Yu always seemed so proper.

375
00:20:50,790 --> 00:20:52,200
Who knew he was like this?

376
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:53,710
No, no.

377
00:20:53,740 --> 00:20:55,340
I can't let Xiaotao team up
with someone like him.

378
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:57,200
I've got to figure something out.

379
00:20:59,770 --> 00:21:01,780
We'll continue our discussion tomorrow

380
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:03,780
at 2 p.m. at the café by the west gate.

381
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:32,570
Aren't they here yet?

382
00:21:54,430 --> 00:21:56,160
How's your preparation going?

383
00:21:58,110 --> 00:21:59,840
I still haven't figured it out.

384
00:22:07,970 --> 00:22:09,320
You're a junior.

385
00:22:09,650 --> 00:22:13,050
What made you decide to take
a freshman course all of a sudden?

386
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:17,720
I think

387
00:22:18,550 --> 00:22:20,610
I think my reason is the same as yours.

388
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:34,080
Sorry we're late.

389
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:36,200
It's okay. We just got here, too.

390
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:47,010
What would you like to drink?

391
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:48,200
It's on me today.

392
00:22:48,310 --> 00:22:49,240
I'll go with you.

393
00:22:49,850 --> 00:22:50,640
Let's go.

394
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:05,960
Senior, have you
found any inspiration yet?

395
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:10,840
Still thinking.

396
00:23:30,530 --> 00:23:31,740
Here's your coffee.

397
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:33,090
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

398
00:23:46,990 --> 00:23:47,880
Let me.

399
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,220
The coffee's here.

400
00:24:00,550 --> 00:24:01,600
Xiangxiang.

401
00:24:04,090 --> 00:24:05,640
Here you go. And here you go.

402
00:24:05,860 --> 00:24:07,040
Thank you.

403
00:24:07,630 --> 00:24:08,440
Thank you.

404
00:24:19,140 --> 00:24:21,840
Why don't we keep talking about poetry?

405
00:24:21,870 --> 00:24:24,000
I've just found some new inspiration.

406
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,220
What inspiration?

407
00:24:25,220 --> 00:24:27,820
Director, I think this is
a great opportunity.

408
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:31,020
Fang Yu.

409
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:32,800
Director.

410
00:24:33,550 --> 00:24:34,690
I was just looking for you.

411
00:24:34,690 --> 00:24:35,680
Are you free later?

412
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:36,990
Let's grab a meal together.

413
00:24:36,990 --> 00:24:37,830
A meal?

414
00:24:38,290 --> 00:24:39,290
What for?

415
00:24:40,560 --> 00:24:41,660
Sirui can connect us

416
00:24:41,660 --> 00:24:43,140
with some students

417
00:24:43,170 --> 00:24:44,300
from other schools.

418
00:24:44,380 --> 00:24:46,490
We could bring
our basketball team together

419
00:24:46,490 --> 00:24:48,550
with a few well-known teams
outside the school

420
00:24:48,550 --> 00:24:50,390
and put together a show.

421
00:24:50,610 --> 00:24:51,770
It'd be a great hit.

422
00:24:53,770 --> 00:24:55,900
Basketball teams from other schools?

423
00:24:58,990 --> 00:24:59,790
That's right.

424
00:25:02,650 --> 00:25:03,710
Does it have to be now?

425
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:04,700
I still have something I need to—

426
00:25:04,700 --> 00:25:05,540
Fang Yu,

427
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:06,760
this is important.

428
00:25:06,790 --> 00:25:07,940
It concerns the campus TV station

429
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:10,180
and the plans
of several university basketball teams.

430
00:25:10,180 --> 00:25:11,500
We need your input.

431
00:25:20,150 --> 00:25:21,790
Li Sirui, hurry up and go.

432
00:25:21,810 --> 00:25:23,420
We're discussing our assignment here.

433
00:25:23,420 --> 00:25:25,020
I'm saving you, okay?

434
00:25:25,540 --> 00:25:26,820
What's wrong with you?

435
00:25:27,930 --> 00:25:28,810
Well,

436
00:25:29,060 --> 00:25:30,580
how about we meet another day?

437
00:25:30,580 --> 00:25:31,820
It's okay, Senior.

438
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,240
We can meet another time.

439
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:37,490
I'm really sorry.

440
00:25:37,490 --> 00:25:38,820
Let's meet another day.

441
00:25:39,490 --> 00:25:40,470
Then let's go.

442
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:42,440
Senior, the lecturer said we need

443
00:25:42,450 --> 00:25:43,530
to spend more time together

444
00:25:43,530 --> 00:25:44,690
to find inspiration.

445
00:25:44,690 --> 00:25:45,880
So, mind if I tag along

446
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:47,010
for dinner tonight?

447
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:49,960
No problem. Come along.

448
00:25:50,070 --> 00:25:51,030
Thanks, Senior.

449
00:25:53,540 --> 00:25:54,260
I'm off.

450
00:25:56,300 --> 00:25:58,020
Let's go eat.

451
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:10,340
So...

452
00:26:11,360 --> 00:26:12,240
where were we?

453
00:26:24,580 --> 00:26:25,420
Sirui,

454
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:28,640
didn't you say players from other schools

455
00:26:28,640 --> 00:26:29,720
were joining us?

456
00:26:29,740 --> 00:26:31,140
Why aren't they here yet?

457
00:26:31,610 --> 00:26:32,250
Director,

458
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:35,310
although this gathering
was put together at the last minute

459
00:26:35,310 --> 00:26:37,370
and not everyone could make it today,

460
00:26:37,380 --> 00:26:38,940
Let's eat first.

461
00:26:40,460 --> 00:26:42,820
Let me say a few words
on behalf of our team.

462
00:26:43,170 --> 00:26:44,760
Ever since I joined the basketball team,

463
00:26:44,760 --> 00:26:46,600
I've watched our fan base grow

464
00:26:46,620 --> 00:26:48,620
and our profile rise

465
00:26:48,650 --> 00:26:49,810
year after year.

466
00:26:49,990 --> 00:26:51,300
Honestly, we owe a lot of that

467
00:26:51,300 --> 00:26:53,000
to the campus TV station's
extensive promotion,

468
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:56,200
especially Fang Yu's
hard work and dedication.

469
00:26:56,730 --> 00:26:58,390
Fang Yu, I'd like to toast you.

470
00:27:05,140 --> 00:27:06,870
You're too kind, Sirui.

471
00:27:06,890 --> 00:27:08,620
It's what we're supposed to do.

472
00:27:14,160 --> 00:27:15,120
Li Sirui.

473
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:17,920
Sit down. No need to be so formal.

474
00:27:26,810 --> 00:27:28,390
Here, use this.

475
00:27:28,450 --> 00:27:29,380
Thanks, Senior.

476
00:27:31,930 --> 00:27:32,570
Fang Yu,

477
00:27:33,040 --> 00:27:35,170
Le Xiaotao is the only girl here today.

478
00:27:35,500 --> 00:27:37,230
Don't you think you should
have a drink with her, too?

479
00:27:37,230 --> 00:27:38,070
Li Sirui,

480
00:27:38,100 --> 00:27:39,340
that's enough.

481
00:27:39,360 --> 00:27:42,010
I still have to discuss our assignment
with Senior tomorrow.

482
00:27:42,010 --> 00:27:42,690
It's okay.

483
00:27:42,710 --> 00:27:44,330
If you can't hold your liquor,
you don't have to drink.

484
00:27:44,330 --> 00:27:46,290
Li Sirui, cut it out.

485
00:27:50,850 --> 00:27:51,770
Thank you.

486
00:27:53,030 --> 00:27:56,000
I barely got any work done for our
classical Chinese class this afternoon.

487
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:59,560
You spent the whole time helping me
choose a topic for my documentary.

488
00:27:59,560 --> 00:28:00,200
It's fine.

489
00:28:00,470 --> 00:28:01,710
Didn't the lecturer say

490
00:28:01,710 --> 00:28:04,710
we'd get more inspiration
by spending time together?

491
00:28:08,660 --> 00:28:10,090
My foundation in classical Chinese
is so weak.

492
00:28:10,090 --> 00:28:12,090
Why did you choose to team up with me?

493
00:28:12,850 --> 00:28:13,930
Well, you helped me

494
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:15,380
with market research, too.

495
00:28:15,380 --> 00:28:17,240
I don't like owing people favors.

496
00:28:20,690 --> 00:28:22,950
How's the basketball team doing lately?

497
00:28:23,950 --> 00:28:25,150
We're short a center,

498
00:28:25,550 --> 00:28:27,880
so our games
haven't been going very well.

499
00:28:28,620 --> 00:28:29,750
Zhou Yunze?

500
00:28:35,430 --> 00:28:37,400
Well, it's normal for teammates

501
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,660
to have some friction.

502
00:28:38,970 --> 00:28:40,170
Take us, for example.

503
00:28:40,660 --> 00:28:41,820
If you hadn't been so patient

504
00:28:41,820 --> 00:28:44,180
with me in market research,

505
00:28:44,580 --> 00:28:46,110
I wouldn't have helped you.

506
00:28:53,340 --> 00:28:56,340
Actually, I've seen him

507
00:28:56,980 --> 00:28:59,510
practicing under the blazing sun
many times.

508
00:29:00,060 --> 00:29:01,140
I think

509
00:29:01,820 --> 00:29:03,880
he must really love basketball, too.

510
00:29:10,460 --> 00:29:12,060
I haven't asked you this yet.

511
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:14,990
Why did you choose
our classical Chinese course?

512
00:29:19,020 --> 00:29:20,860
I wanted to get some credits
out of the way.

513
00:29:20,860 --> 00:29:22,140
I'll have training later on,

514
00:29:22,140 --> 00:29:24,000
and I'm worried I won't have time.

515
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:29,700
Let's go.

516
00:29:34,980 --> 00:29:36,020
Be careful.

517
00:29:42,700 --> 00:29:43,980
I just don't get it.

518
00:29:44,100 --> 00:29:46,160
What did Fang Yu ever do to offend you?

519
00:29:46,980 --> 00:29:48,700
I just can't stand him.

520
00:29:49,660 --> 00:29:51,620
He acts like such a gentleman,

521
00:29:52,380 --> 00:29:54,510
but when he writes poetry for someone,

522
00:29:54,620 --> 00:29:56,500
it's all about untying perfume pouches

523
00:29:56,500 --> 00:29:58,060
and loosening sashes.

524
00:29:58,500 --> 00:29:59,580
What a creep.

525
00:30:00,580 --> 00:30:02,580
So you got him drunk

526
00:30:03,180 --> 00:30:04,500
for my sake?

527
00:30:06,380 --> 00:30:07,420
I was just

528
00:30:08,220 --> 00:30:09,550
standing up for justice

529
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:11,920
and coming to your rescue.

530
00:30:12,860 --> 00:30:14,540
Alright. Come on, let's go.

531
00:30:14,540 --> 00:30:15,600
I'll walk you back.

532
00:30:16,140 --> 00:30:16,820
Be careful.

533
00:30:17,740 --> 00:30:19,060
Standing up for justice...

534
00:30:19,060 --> 00:30:21,860
-And coming to your rescue.
-All right, all right.

535
00:30:24,220 --> 00:30:25,060
So none of the centers

536
00:30:25,060 --> 00:30:26,620
who came to try out recently

537
00:30:26,660 --> 00:30:27,620
were a good fit?

538
00:30:27,780 --> 00:30:29,410
[Pei Tian]

539
00:30:35,100 --> 00:30:36,900
Some are tall but lack footwork,

540
00:30:36,980 --> 00:30:38,900
while others have good footwork
but lack physicality.

541
00:30:38,900 --> 00:30:40,540
None really fit our system.

542
00:30:45,420 --> 00:30:46,380
Zhou Yunze?

543
00:30:47,140 --> 00:30:49,780
Actually, I've seen him practicing

544
00:30:50,620 --> 00:30:52,940
under the blazing sun many times.

545
00:30:53,860 --> 00:30:54,780
I think

546
00:30:55,420 --> 00:30:57,480
he must really love basketball, too.

547
00:31:08,070 --> 00:31:10,120
[Jiangcheng University]

548
00:31:10,180 --> 00:31:16,310
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

549
00:31:15,300 --> 00:31:15,860
Come on.

550
00:31:20,340 --> 00:31:21,020
Come on.

551
00:31:28,680 --> 00:31:31,470
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

552
00:31:31,020 --> 00:31:31,780
Sirui,

553
00:31:32,860 --> 00:31:34,720
how much did you drink yesterday?

554
00:31:36,100 --> 00:31:36,860
Don't ask.

555
00:31:36,980 --> 00:31:38,840
I skipped all my morning classes.

556
00:31:39,220 --> 00:31:40,700
What did you do to Xiaotao?

557
00:31:41,980 --> 00:31:42,780
Nothing.

558
00:31:46,730 --> 00:31:48,220
She had us come downstairs

559
00:31:48,220 --> 00:31:49,500
first thing in the morning

560
00:31:49,500 --> 00:31:51,060
to pick up all this stuff.

561
00:31:51,060 --> 00:31:54,060
She said it was to help you
recover from your hangover.

562
00:31:59,220 --> 00:32:02,480
Just a friend looking out for a friend.
What's the big deal?

563
00:32:04,270 --> 00:32:05,670
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

564
00:32:04,860 --> 00:32:05,860
Go practice.

565
00:32:12,700 --> 00:32:13,380
Come on.

566
00:32:20,380 --> 00:32:21,060
Hurry up!

567
00:32:21,060 --> 00:32:21,980
Coming, coming!

568
00:32:21,980 --> 00:32:23,710
One more round, one more round!

569
00:32:24,460 --> 00:32:25,540
How did I die again?

570
00:32:25,420 --> 00:32:25,940
[Friend Request Message]

571
00:32:25,700 --> 00:32:26,820
Staff! Staff!

572
00:32:27,670 --> 00:32:28,410
[Friend Request Message]

573
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:29,720
Happy Rascal.

574
00:32:28,470 --> 00:32:29,390
[Friend Request]

575
00:32:33,220 --> 00:32:33,900
Accept.

576
00:32:36,140 --> 00:32:36,940
Who are you?

577
00:32:38,820 --> 00:32:40,660
Your username looked a lot like mine,

578
00:32:40,660 --> 00:32:42,320
so I sent you a friend request.

579
00:32:42,740 --> 00:32:44,940
But you're "Happy," and I'm "Sad."

580
00:32:45,130 --> 00:32:47,550
[Happy Rascal]

581
00:32:45,620 --> 00:32:46,980
Are you a guy or a girl?

582
00:32:50,500 --> 00:32:51,180
A guy.

583
00:32:51,670 --> 00:32:54,790
[Happy Rascal]

584
00:32:52,540 --> 00:32:55,020
Why would a guy use such a girly username?

585
00:32:57,980 --> 00:32:58,940
You got me.

586
00:33:28,070 --> 00:33:30,450
[Happy Rascal]

587
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:34,560
[Was your account hacked?
Why haven't you been online?]

588
00:33:34,580 --> 00:33:35,550
[If you're online,
I'll help you win some games.]

589
00:33:35,570 --> 00:33:36,850
[Let me know when you're online.]

590
00:33:41,630 --> 00:33:43,980
[Happy Rascal]
[The owner has restricted access.]

591
00:33:51,260 --> 00:33:52,300
Sun Yi!

592
00:33:54,260 --> 00:33:55,820
Go for it, Sun Yi! Go for it, Sun Yi!

593
00:33:55,820 --> 00:33:57,680
-Go for it, Sun Yi!
-Pass the ball!

594
00:33:58,420 --> 00:33:59,580
Go for it, Sun Yi!

595
00:33:59,780 --> 00:34:00,860
Han Zhen!

596
00:34:06,580 --> 00:34:08,710
Zhou Yunze, what's with the attitude?

597
00:34:08,860 --> 00:34:10,580
Show some respect for basketball.

598
00:34:10,580 --> 00:34:11,580
What the hell?

599
00:34:12,060 --> 00:34:14,179
Basketball isn't a tool for showing off.

600
00:34:14,179 --> 00:34:15,699
It's about teamwork.

601
00:34:16,380 --> 00:34:17,460
Are you nuts?

602
00:34:17,620 --> 00:34:18,550
What did you say?

603
00:34:19,489 --> 00:34:20,860
-Don't fight!
-Let go!

604
00:34:23,900 --> 00:34:24,929
You act so tough, don't you?

605
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:26,179
Got the guts to face me in a game?

606
00:34:26,179 --> 00:34:27,179
What kind of game?

607
00:34:27,260 --> 00:34:28,699
You love passing the ball, don't you?

608
00:34:28,699 --> 00:34:30,139
With all these teammates here,

609
00:34:30,139 --> 00:34:31,139
pick one.

610
00:34:33,060 --> 00:34:34,650
Well, don't blame us for this.

611
00:34:34,650 --> 00:34:37,100
You're always preaching about teamwork,

612
00:34:37,100 --> 00:34:39,460
but now you can't even find a teammate
to play with.

613
00:34:39,460 --> 00:34:40,940
Aren't you embarrassed?

614
00:34:44,820 --> 00:34:45,500
I'll do it.
